Microsoft ( MSFT ) CFO Amy Hood told analysts on October 28 that the company has access to the debt markets but “we haven’t yet, I would say, tapped that.” Bloomberg reported a deal in the works on October 29, and that evening Microsoft priced $25 billion of senior unsecured notes in ten tranches maturing from 2028 to 2066, its first U.S. investment-grade bond sale since 2017, per Bloomberg. Shares closed down 0.16% that day, giving back an after-hours jump of about 4% on 48% Azure growth, as Alphabet tumbled after its own report.
